= Measurement — Simple =

'''Measurement''' is a careful way of finding a value for some property of a thing.

Examples:

* measuring length;
* measuring temperature;
* measuring voltage;
* measuring mass.

Good measurement is more than reading a number from an instrument.

You need to know:

* What exactly are you measuring?
* Which unit are you using?
* Was the instrument calibrated?
* How much [[Uncertainty/Simple|uncertainty]] is there?
* Under what conditions was the measurement made?

Two important ideas are [[Accuracy and precision/Simple|accuracy and precision]].

Accuracy is about closeness to the right/reference value.

Precision is about how closely repeated measurements agree with each other.

A measurement can be very precise but still wrong in the same direction every time.

